 "mechanism": {
  "default": "absent key = every committed configuration = the dispatch exactly as before; the parser refuses unknown keys, a wrong schema, non-boolean switches and a block that arms nothing",
  "dependency_verified": "1b is POSSIBLE for the recall and IMPOSSIBLE for the rest: the exemplar recall's inputs are the frozen snapshot, the row's own sealed speech query record and the key vectors (rails.phase_supply supply_for_phase -> KbFacetProvider.candidates -> multidim_recall), none of which is the Perception answer; the rank, fusion and the candidate-bound slot-contract selection (candidate_supply.solver, candidate_state_phase perception) DO read the sealed Perception state and stay exactly where they are.",
  "finding": "Rows in flight already exceed the slots (queue depth 4 x slots = 16 admitted rows over 4 slots), but every admitted row is pinned to one llama.cpp slot from its first contact to its delivery, because 88.9 % of the flown prompt tokens are served from that slot's KV prefix; releasing a slot between contacts would re-prefill a row's whole supply block (about 7,500 tokens, 3.3 s) to save a 0.5 s gap. The slots therefore empty while their OWN row prepares the next contact. The largest part of that preparation is the first Solver visit's role input: settle -> the train-exemplars recall (rails.kb_policy.multidim_recall, a pure-Python cosine over every exemplar key vector) -> material, run synchronously in the OpenJiuwen role-query component on the ONE asyncio event loop every row shares, so while one row recalls, no other row can route or dispatch; full garbage collections over the loaded key vectors freeze every thread at once.",
  "switches": {
   "gc_freeze": "gc.collect(); gc.freeze() before the first episode, gc.unfreeze() after the last",
   "recall_prefetch": "the row's Perception-independent recall submitted to one background worker at admission; the Solver visit consumes it through the provider's existing prepared-recall path; a revisit recomputes live",
   "role_input_offload": "the role-input builder awaited on ONE dedicated worker thread (role inputs stay mutually exclusive across rows, the calling task's context variables carried over)"
  }
 },
